### Step 2: The Application CRD Manifest (`guestbook-app.yaml`)

The `Application` Custom Resource is the foundational building block of ArgoCD. It ties together:
1. **Where manifests live** (Source Git repository)
2. **Where they should run** (Destination cluster & namespace)
3. **How they should be synced** (Sync policy & options)

Save the following complete YAML as `guestbook-app.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: guestbook
  namespace: argocd
  finalizers:
    - resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io
spec:
  # The project this application belongs to (default provides unrestricted access)
  project: default

  # Source: Where the desired state lives in Git
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/argoproj/argocd-example-apps.git
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: guestbook

  # Destination: Where to deploy the resources in Kubernetes
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: guestbook

  # Sync policy: Manual sync with automatic namespace creation safeguard
  syncPolicy:
    syncOptions:
      - CreateNamespace=true
```

