### Step 5: Inspect Pre-Sync State (Why OutOfSync & Missing is Normal)

Immediately after applying the CRD, ArgoCD connects to Git, renders the manifests, and checks the cluster.

Run the inspection commands:

```bash
# 1. View status with kubectl
kubectl get application guestbook -n argocd

# 2. View full details with ArgoCD CLI
argocd app get guestbook
```

*Actual Output from `kubectl get application guestbook -n argocd`:*
```text
NAME        SYNC STATUS   HEALTH STATUS
guestbook   OutOfSync     Missing
```

*Actual Output from `argocd app get guestbook`:*
```text
Name:               argocd/guestbook
Project:            default
Server:             https://kubernetes.default.svc
Namespace:          guestbook
URL:                https://localhost:8080/applications/guestbook
Source:
- Repo:             https://github.com/argoproj/argocd-example-apps.git
  Target:           HEAD
  Path:             guestbook
SyncWindow:         Sync Allowed
Sync Policy:        Manual
Sync Status:        OutOfSync from HEAD (8088f4c)
Health Status:      Missing

GROUP  KIND        NAMESPACE  NAME          STATUS     HEALTH   HOOK  MESSAGE
       Service     guestbook  guestbook-ui  OutOfSync  Missing        
apps   Deployment  guestbook  guestbook-ui  OutOfSync  Missing        
```

> 📌 **Read the output carefully — four things differ from older ArgoCD releases:**
> | Field | Older docs show | Current output |
> | :--- | :--- | :--- |
> | `Name` | `guestbook` | `argocd/guestbook` — now namespace-qualified |
> | `Repo`/`Target`/`Path` | three flat fields | nested under a `Source:` **list** (multi-source support) |
> | `Sync Policy` | `<none>` | `Manual` |
> | `SyncWindow` | absent | `Sync Allowed` |
>
> The commit SHA (`8088f4c` here) is whatever `HEAD` of the upstream example repo points at on the day you run the lab — yours will differ, and that is fine. Resources are also listed `Service` before `Deployment`.

#### 🔍 Why are these statuses normal?
- **Sync Status: `OutOfSync` (Yellow Badge):** Git declares that a `Deployment` and a `Service` should exist. But nothing exists in the `guestbook` namespace yet. Desired State ≠ Live State.
- **Health Status: `Missing` (Grey Heart):** Because the Deployment and Service have not been applied to Kubernetes, their health cannot be determined.

Open your browser to `https://localhost:8080`:
- You will see the **guestbook** card with a yellow badge (`OutOfSync`) and a grey heart (`Missing`).

