### Step 6: Trigger Manual Sync & Watch Live Reconciliation

Now trigger the sync operation to reconcile Git into the cluster:

```bash
# Trigger sync. This BLOCKS until the sync operation completes.
argocd app sync guestbook
```

> 🛑 **There is no `--watch` flag on `argocd app sync`.** Earlier versions of this lab used `argocd app sync guestbook --watch`, which now fails outright:
> ```text
> Error: unknown flag: --watch
> ```
> `argocd app sync` **already waits** for the operation to finish — that is the default. The flag you would reach for is the inverse, `--async`, which returns immediately without waiting. `--wait` does not exist either. Verify the real flag list yourself with `argocd app sync --help`.

*Actual Output (trimmed to the tail):*
```text
Sync Status:        Synced to HEAD (8088f4c)
Health Status:      Progressing

Operation:          Sync
Sync Revision:      8088f4c0d970abb09e250248cc97e35623447cb5
Phase:              Succeeded
Start:              2026-09-26 15:18:29 +0000 UTC
Finished:           2026-09-26 15:18:30 +0000 UTC
Duration:           1s
Message:            successfully synced (all tasks run)

GROUP  KIND        NAMESPACE  NAME          STATUS  HEALTH       HOOK  MESSAGE
       Service     guestbook  guestbook-ui  Synced  Healthy            service/guestbook-ui created
apps   Deployment  guestbook  guestbook-ui  Synced  Progressing        deployment.apps/guestbook-ui created
```

Notice the sync itself finished in **1 second**, but health is still `Progressing` — the *sync* succeeded while the Deployment's pods were still starting. Sync completion and health convergence are two separate events.

#### Blocking until the app is actually Healthy
To wait for health rather than just sync, use the dedicated `wait` subcommand:
```bash
argocd app wait guestbook --health --timeout 180
```
*Actual Output:*
```text
Sync Status:        Synced to HEAD (8088f4c)
Health Status:      Healthy

GROUP  KIND        NAMESPACE  NAME          STATUS  HEALTH   HOOK  MESSAGE
       Service     guestbook  guestbook-ui  Synced  Healthy        service/guestbook-ui created
apps   Deployment  guestbook  guestbook-ui  Synced  Healthy        deployment.apps/guestbook-ui created
```

Check the final application status:
```bash
argocd app get guestbook
```
```text
Sync Status:        Synced to HEAD (8088f4c)
Health Status:      Healthy
```

