## 📝 Quick Reference Command Cheat Sheet

Keep these commands handy during your GitOps workflows:

```bash
# Cluster & Pre-flight (run all of these in WSL2)
kubectl get nodes
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready node --all --timeout=180s
kubectl get pods -n argocd
kubectl -n argocd wait --for=condition=available deployment --all --timeout=600s
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443

# CLI authentication (required before any argocd command)
PW=$(kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d)
argocd login localhost:8080 --username admin --password "$PW" --insecure
argocd version --short

# Application Management
kubectl apply -f guestbook-app.yaml
kubectl get application guestbook -n argocd
argocd app get guestbook
argocd app list

# Sync Operations  (NOTE: no --watch and no --wait flag exists on sync)
argocd app sync guestbook                      # blocks until sync completes
argocd app sync guestbook --async              # return immediately, don't wait
argocd app wait guestbook --health             # block until Healthy
argocd app sync guestbook --dry-run            # preview without applying

# Drift Detection & Refresh  (NOTE: 'argocd app refresh' is NOT a subcommand)
argocd app diff guestbook                      # exits 1 when drift exists
argocd app get guestbook --refresh             # re-read Git
argocd app get guestbook --hard-refresh        # re-read Git, bust manifest cache

# Application Workloads
kubectl get all -n guestbook
kubectl port-forward -n guestbook svc/guestbook-ui 8081:80
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" http://localhost:8081
kubectl scale deployment guestbook-ui --replicas=4 -n guestbook

# Cleanup
kubectl delete -f guestbook-app.yaml
kubectl delete namespace guestbook
```

